# Tenant, privacy, public code

Tenant is a **security boundary**. Every query and mutation is tenant-scoped: devices, MACs, IPs, collection runs, history, correlation, API, MCP.

A tenant must never receive another tenant's observations. New/changed endpoints need a **cross-tenant** test when they return data.

## Data minimization

Prefer dropping out-of-scope evidence **before** persisting endpoint observations.

Exclusion policy is **runtime / private configuration**, never hardcoded in this public repo:

- no customer names
- no real VLAN IDs or “student VLAN” mappings
- no real networks, IPs, or “this OLT is Y”

Future filters (exclude VLAN / network / device / observation class) must be testable and auditable **without** storing the excluded payload.

## No client knowledge in code

Public/generic code must not encode operational facts that belong in tenant config:

- which router is the DHCP server
- which VLAN is which role
- which OLT belongs to which site
- management networks, real hostnames, customer names

## Fixtures

Versioned fixtures are **synthetic**. Do not paste real customer CLI and change one field. Preserve device syntax; use artificial identifiers.

## Logs

Structured when practical. Sanitize. No secrets, no unnecessary private command output. Tenant/device IDs only when policy allows. Collection runs are core product observability.
